fluxecho.module.mana_fountain=Mana Fountain Array
tile.fluxecho.module_core.mana_fountain.name=Mana Fountain Array Core
fluxecho.mana_fountain.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's fountain court§r\nA cloister round a court of fountains and a magic circle, a spout of mana rising from its obelisk\nIts fountains and flower urns keep the team's Botania samples; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.mana_fountain.structure=§bThe Mana Fountain Array: an octagonal cloister 25×25 and 8 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on a diagonal pavilion site (site 1 first, then 7, 3, 5) once the Mana Fountain Array is researched (phase II): the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start\n· Four chamfer portals lead under a glass-roofed arcade and through a colonnade into an open court with a magic circle; the arcade's floor is grass for your own flowers and mana pools, and the obelisk's top gives way to a rendered spout of mana once it forms\n· 16 units, 16 samples: 8 fountains (a Sample Socket over the water in a ring of Basin Rims) and 8 flower urns; a unit is used as a whole: right-click any part of it holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the array; sneak-click a socket empty-handed to take its sample back\n· The core on the obelisk's Console Stand at the court's centre, two blocks above the foundation\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck and Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, posts, plinths, Basin Rims, Sample Sockets, water and Cladding Anchors (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
